---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy and cookie settings | WalStack" description="How I handle PostgreSQL snapshot files, enquiries, campaign tags and cookie-free website analytics.">
  <header class="container hero"><h1>How I handle your information</h1><p class="lede">Review your files before sharing them. I only need database statistics and a short description of the problem.</p></header>
  <section><div class="container prose"><h2>Free snapshot reviews</h2>
    <p>I use the output and optional screenshot only to write your findings. Formspree receives the form and stores the attachments for me. I use your email address to send the review.</p>
    <p>I keep the output private. I delete the files from Formspree and my working copies after {site.retentionDays} days unless you hire me. If you hire me, I agree data handling with you in writing.</p>
    <p>Remove credentials, customer data and sensitive text before sending files. To ask me to delete a snapshot sooner, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    <h2>Enquiries and calls</h2><p>I use the details you send to reply. The contact form uses Formspree when enabled. Booking links take you to Cal.com, where you choose a time and provide your contact details.</p>
    <h2 id="cookies">Cookie settings</h2><p>I use Plausible to count visits, downloads, accepted snapshot submissions and clicks. It uses no analytics cookies. I don't send form answers, email addresses, filenames or file contents to analytics.</p>
    <p>When you follow a tagged link, this browser tab remembers the campaign and page where you arrived. I include that context with your form so I can tell which introductions lead to requests. Closing the tab clears it.</p>
    <p>For questions about your information, contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
